A||||8||Richard Parnell||Fascia Repair again||||7||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||03-01-2000||03:09 PM||||Sorry to keep on about this subject.  When I try to do a search I get a URL not found on everything I've searched for lately.  So I need someone's help to get a thread to the item I saw a while back.  It was details on how to repair cracked fascias.  Any help will be greatly appreciated.  I don't want to have to order a new front fascia if I can repair the one I have. Thanks||||reg||7
Z||000001||deceler8||03-01-2000||03:15 PM||||I've always heard the best way to repair a damaged fascia is to reinforce the crack at the rear with fiberglass cloth and fillin the crack with body filler.<P>Seems there are also kits available to repair cracks/tears in flexible fascias at most auto parts stores, but I suspect that the kit consists of the above items.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-01-2000||04:08 PM||||Just make sure you get the flexible filler.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||03-01-2000||04:40 PM||||So many cars today have the flexible bumper covers, I'd be willing to bet that most any autobody repair shop should be able to repair damaged facia.  I had a tear in the rear bumper of my new Buick Regal.  It was repaired and I can't even see the weld seam or how it got put back together, even looking at the underside.<P>If the fasia is off the car take it to some reparable auto body shop and ask.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 03-01-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-01-2000||04:42 PM||||Or get a plastic welder.  I think JCWhitney has them.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87SC/GT||03-01-2000||05:11 PM||||I've had good success welding them with a soldering iron. You need to use the same material for filler material. I took a trashed Gt nose and cut it into thin strips to use as filler. The fiberglass reinforcement is a good safety  precaution. Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-01-2000||06:39 PM||||What about using Super Glue and Silly Putty?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phaeton||03-01-2000||11:01 PM||||Dang it Monkeyman, I wish you would tell me when you're just joking.  Now my fascia bounced and stuck to a garage rafter, and my ladder is still under the snow.  At least I'd finished erasing the stripes first.||||reg||11
Z||000008||Monkeyman||03-02-2000||07:04 AM||||Ummm...Sorry.  I was just joking.  Look on the bright side.  If you cut the rafter that your fascia is on and bring it into the living room, you'll have a heck of a conversation piece! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
